00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
on this international women's day we  take the opportunity to honor female  accomplishments but we also pause to  consider the struggles and universal  challenges that women face globally  one of those struggles is of course  gender-based violence women face this  every day both on and offline digital  violence can include things like cyber  stalking hate speech and the  non-consensual use of photos and videos  which of course has lasting consequences  on women and girls our next guest frames  this as a human rights abuse issue dr  natalia connem is executive director of  the united nations population fund an  agency that's dedicated to sexual and  reproductive health rights for women and  girls dr and welcome to quick take we're  going to dive into how your agency is  helping on the issue of digital violence  but we'd be remiss if we didn't start  with asking you about what's going on  with women and girls as they flee  ukraine  women and children being separated from  the men who are being kept to fight what  is your single biggest concern right now  for the women and girls who are fleeing  the impact of conflict on women and  girls is heartbreaking and it is really  dangerous and i'm preoccupied by the  understanding that at this very moment  the majority of people fleeing out of  harm's way are women and they're  children and they're vulnerable they  need protection  by the way  it's important also to understand that  within the next three months  about 80 000 ukrainian women who are  pregnant will be giving birth and during  those three months they need their  health care they need protection and  they need to be able to deliver safely  while giving life  we also see  pictures and videos of women giving  birth in abandoned subway stations in  kiev at the moment as well so there are  women who are staying behind in ukraine  what are ngos like the u.n agency that  you work for doing to ensure their  safety especially when you can't or your  monitors can't always be physically  present all the  time me highlight that the united  nations as an organization of  multilaterals  not governmental but working with all  governments has played a really  important role  in doing two things secretary general  antonio guterres has called for peace  for ceasefire for an immediate  succession of the hostilities which are  the reason that women and girls are on  the run and i'm talking to the tune of  two million people who have left ukraine  in such a short space of time  the second thing that multilateral  organizations such as unfpa which is the  sexual and reproductive health agency  hence our concern for pregnant women for  violence which shadows women when they  are fleeing and i'm i'm speaking of  gender-based violence up to and  including rape and these concerns of  trafficking that can occur in these uh  crises  however when it comes to assuring you  know it's winter food is an issue the un  is working in concert on issues of  transport and again insisting on the  fundamentals of peace dialogue as a way  to resolve issues  yeah we've seen a lot of video footage  of children uh fleeing on their own  without any appearance of parents in  sight dr connum what can be done to keep  those children safe specifically girls  who are crossing on their own and and  may not have any form of parental uh  guidance or or assistance with them to  kind of keep them safe how can they be  kept safe then  again i insist on full respect for women  and their concerns and you know this uh  concern for children which unicef also  expresses is an understanding that they  are vulnerable when people are  vulnerable and need protection  everything has to organize in order to  defend their human rights let me tell  you that setting up shelters for people  in crisis right now is so important  during uh  the weather conditions that people are  facing moreover there's the matter of  biology  unfpa provides dignity kits which are  handed out by the midwives by the social  workers by the numerous nurses and  doctors that we employ to shield people  from having biological concerns like  menstruation  um the dignity  contains health  hygiene  uh contents that are very much  appreciated during this time  the other one uh the other point i  really have to make is that the welcome  on the other side of the border is also  something that we're helping with yeah  the neighboring countries uh  also need assistance as they receive the  refugee population  well when we think about gender-based  violence of course digital violence  comes to mind as well and i know that  you and your organization have a big  campaign around that can you tell me a  little bit about what you're doing to  allow women to have agency and control  over their bodies and kind of copyright  their own bodies online that's right  well  it has to be understood that the virtual  space now  is an arena where violence happens and  it is real it is just as real  without borders or limits as something  that happens in the physical space and  often these things spill over and the  question that unfpa is asking in our  body right campaign which we invite  everyone to join  is why should a copyright for a poem or  a book or a song have more weight  than the image of a woman or girl in the  virtual space you're the owner of your  body wherever you are the b with the  circle around it akin to the c for  copyright  means that objectionable images that a  woman or a girl did not consent to  should come down and were asking tech  companies to please understand that  these are human rights violations the  other very important thing is that  bullying online intimidates women and  girls who have every right to  participate in that space so that's what  bodywrite is trying to say loud and  clear my body is my own i'm the owner of  my body right  how much of the burden then falls on the  big tech companies the social media  companies that are in charge of these  platforms when it comes to addressing  this versus  individual bad actors who will find a  way to do this with or without the help  of those platforms  you know this is a great question  because what unfpa is saying  is that there's a system that has to  acknowledge in particular a gender  differential  that makes women and girls vulnerable at  a time when a lot has gone online  because of the pandemic  girls are  learning online hence the type of  intimidation the name calling the types  of insults but also threats and stalking  it's a system that has to respond and  tech companies the power of business the  understanding of regulating that  environment has to privilege women and  girls being safe online  and also to take down images that are up  there without consent  really really important because it has  huge  mental health implications depression  all the way through suicide when people  are attacked relentlessly online and for  women politicians also to be respected  in the virtual space right and women and  girls are of course punished if their  images are posted online without their  consent so it's just a very vicious  cycle dr khanna when we talk about this  and i think about the future of the  internet and i think about the metaverse  i'm more and more concerned about having  another new space to navigate where  we're going to continue to see some of  the bad behavior we've already seen  online follow us into the metaverse what  is your number one biggest concern as we  start to develop spaces and go into  spaces in the metaverse specifically for  women and girls  working assiduously with unfpa in over  150 locations around the world the  bottom line is full respect and full  dignity for women today is international  women's day it's a time for us to look  at each other and to say yes we value  women's participation across the whole  arena and the metaverse indeed the  universe should be a gender equal space  women are highly capable of  uh functioning of leading of running  their business being a teacher whatever  it is that she wants to do  she should not be hampered by the type  of  violence that can occur online and it's  a very intimate type of violence it's a  very intimate type of offense when she  opens her phone  she should not be harassed so ultimately  i believe that we need allies business  is a great ally  men and boys are great allies in  understanding that the online space is  now contiguous with quote unquote real  life so very important to claim your  body right and this is what the website  on bodywrite that unfpa has launched is  saying so please join the movement we  need action on this point  really important reminders on all that  dr condom thank you so much for joining  us that was dr natalia connam executive  director of unfpa speaking with us on  international women's day about this  really important issue

